Id: con011c
Severity: CONFIG
Category: tigris
Check: gen_mounts
Fix: Unmount the hung filesystem or make it answer; raise Tiger_Mount_Timeout if it is merely slow.
References: mount(8); tigerrc

The filesystem is of a local type but did not answer a df request
within Tiger_Mount_Timeout seconds, so the filesystem scan leaves it out
rather than hang on it. This is what a hung FUSE mount or a disk that has
gone away looks like. Unmount it, or make it answer, and run again. Raise
Tiger_Mount_Timeout if the filesystem is merely slow.
